@@ -42,6 +42,34 @@ This is an extension for the AUTOMATIC1111's (and Vladmandic´s) webui that allo
  </details>
  
 **To learn more about the parameters, please refer to our [WIKI](https://github.com/v8hid/infinite-zoom-automatic1111-webui/wiki).**
+
+## Music, keyframes and image zooms
+
+<details>
+  <summary> Click to expand </summary>
+
+### Music & Keyframes tab
+* **Soundtrack**: upload any audio file ffmpeg can read (mp3, wav, flac, ogg, opus, m4a/aac, alac, wma, aiff, ac3, mka, ...) or a video with sound. The finished video contains the soundtrack as AAC. Longer music is cut at the end of the video with a fade-out, shorter music is padded with silence. The file is checked before rendering starts; if adding the sound ever fails, the silent video is still saved.
+* **Keyframes**: paste or upload keyframes from the [audio keyframe generator](https://www.chigozie.co.uk/audio-keyframe-generator/) (Disco, PyTTI or CSV output) or Deforum strings such as `0: (1.00), 12: (1.40)`. Sparse keys are interpolated. Only numbers are read; formulas inside keyframes are never executed.
+  * *Speed multiplier* (default): `1` zooms at the Zoom Speed, `2` twice as fast, `0` pauses.
+  * *Deforum zoom*: `1.00` stands still, `1.02` zooms 2% per frame.
+  * *Keyframes FPS* `0` detects the rate from PyTTI text or from the soundtrack length (the website default is 12); otherwise the video FPS is assumed.
+  * With keyframes the video lasts as long as the keyframes, the number of outpaint steps is calculated automatically ("Total video length" is ignored), frame dupes are not used, and prompt keys still count outpaint steps.
+  * **Analyze keyframes** shows the length, FPS and the zoom steps needed.
+  * **Generate keyframes from the soundtrack** computes the same keyframes as the website (loudness per frame, function `1 + x^4` by default) without leaving the webui.
+
+### IMG tab
+Zoom through your own images instead of prompts. Image 1 is the center of the zoom and the last image the outermost frame (sorted by file name, or reversed). Every image gets the previous frame shrunk into its center by the *zoom factor between images* (2 matches Midjourney Zoom Out 2x, 1.33 its 1.5x button).
+* *AI blend strength* `0`: no AI at all, for ready-made nested sequences.
+* Above `0`: Stable Diffusion repaints a ring across the edge of the pasted center (img2img with the Blend prompt; *Seam width* sets how far it reaches into the next image), bridging the previous image into the next one so unrelated images flow into each other. The previous image's own pixels are then restored with a feathered edge, so it stays sharp.
+
+The IMG zoom uses the Render settings of the Main tab, the Video tab, Music & Keyframes, Mask Blur and Post process. Click **Generate video from images** in the IMG tab. With keyframes, the zoom through the images always fills the whole video: the pace is scaled to the number of images, and the keyframes still decide where it speeds up or slows down. With the LCM sampler, add your LCM LoRA to the Blend prompt too (for example `<lora:LCM_SDXL15:1>`); without it the seams come out gray and smeared. The log panel warns when a render uses the LCM sampler without any LoRA tag.
+
+### Tests
+`tests/` contains unit tests for the keyframe, audio, frame and image helpers:
+`python -m unittest discover -s tests` (from the extension folder, with the webui's Python).
+
+</details>
